{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Tradicionál (Severní Amerika)}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse}
From this [G]valley they say you are [D7]going,
we will [G]miss your bright eyes and sweet [D7]smile,
for they [G]say you are taking the [C]sunshine
that has [D7]brightened our pathway a [G]while.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [D7]love me,
do not [G]hasten to bid me a[D7]dieu,
but re[G]member the Red River [C]Valley
and the [D7]one who has loved you so [G]true.
{end_of_chorus}
